# Data is never committed — with one exception: the two hand-collected context
# CSVs have no machine source, so they ARE the source and they live in git.
# (Six of them now: S8 added two, S9 added anchorages.csv, and S10 added
# emodnet_2021-07_leisure.tsv. That last one IS machine output — but of
# notes/emodnet.py over 723 MB of third-party zips that are deleted again on
# the same run, and it is a published aggregate of somebody else's, 5.7 MB, so
# committing it is what makes sql/62 reproducible without the download.)
# They are named one by one, not matched by `*.csv`: anything else that lands in
# data/context/ is machine output, and a stray `INTO OUTFILE 'data/context/x.csv'`
# off vessel_day would otherwise be one `git add` away from publishing MMSIs.
# Order matters. A negation cannot resurrect a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, hence `data/*` + `!data/context/` rather than a blanket `data/`; and
# the `*.csv` line has to come first, because the last matching pattern wins.
# Note the anchoring change that came with it: `data/` matched a `data`
# directory at ANY depth, `data/*` only the one at the repo root. Nested data
# directories — site/data/ for the S12 build, notes/data/ — are no longer
# ignored by these lines. site/data is wanted in git; the rest is covered by the
# extension patterns above.
*.zip
*.csv
*.parquet
*.pmtiles
data/*
!data/context/
data/context/*
!data/context/storms.csv
!data/context/regattas.csv
!data/context/ferry_lines.csv
!data/context/ferry_timetable.csv
!data/context/anchorages.csv
!data/context/emodnet_2021-07_leisure.tsv

# local tooling
.venv/
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store

